    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An aristocratic merchant republic centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubrovnik">Dubrovnik</a>, independent in practice from 1358 to 1808.</li><li>It traded Balkan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and lead and had one of the largest merchant fleets in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> in the 16th century.</li><li>It kept its freedom by paying tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, staying neutral and governing itself through noble councils.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rector-of-ragusa">Rector of Ragusa</a> served for just one month and could not leave his palace during that time except on official business, so that no one could gain personal power.</p></aside>
    </section>

